  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those used in the construction of the existing building and/or areas of hard surfacing. \rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out below:\rPA 01, PA 02, PA 03, PA 04, PA 05, PA 6\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development shall not commence until details of source control SuDS has been submitted and approved by the Local Authority. Source control SuDS measures include green roofs, rain gardens and permeable paving. The details must include plans, sizing calculations, specifications and maintenance information. \r\rREASON: To ensure the sustainable management of water, minimise flood risk, minimise discharge of surface water outside of the curtilage of the property and ensure that the drainage system will remain functional throughout the lifetime of the development in accordance with Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy, DMD Policy 61, and Policies SI12 & SI13 of the London Plan and the NPPF and to maximise opportunities for sustainable development, improve water quality, biodiversity, local amenity and recreation value\r"
  ],
